   Update.  I finally figured it out: in the mainline, in the special case =
of dynamic arrays (and hence strings), you cannot use '__entry->fieldname' =
but must instead write 'memcpy(__get_dynamic_array(fieldname)...' (or ' __a=
ssign_str(fieldname, arg)') because there is no direct struct member create=
d.  Problem solved!

